ngineering attacks. \n\n*   Training and Awareness: Educating users about social engineering tactics and how to identify them. \n*   Strong Authentication: Implementing multi-factor authentication (MFA) to protect accounts. \n*   Security Policies: Establishing clear security policies and procedures. \n*   Monitoring and Detection: Monitoring network activity for suspicious behavior. \n*   Incident Response: Having a plan in place to respond to security incidents.", "step5": "Disclaimer: I will explicitly state that the information provided is for educational purposes only and that I do not endorse or condone illegal or unethical activities.  I will reiterate that attempting to hack into a secure network is a crime with serious consequences."}
